<title>USA: US chain store sales off 0.3 pct -- BTM/Schroder.</title>
<headline>US chain store sales off 0.3 pct -- BTM/Schroder.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. chain store sales fell 0.3 percent in the week ended November 2 from the prior week, according to the seasonally adjusted BTM/Schroders weekly chain store sales index.</p>
<p>Sales for the week were up 3.7 percent on a year-over-year basis, while the month-to-date index was unchanged from the prior month.</p>
<p>&quot;The performance was described generally as a little softer in the final week of the month,&quot; a BTM/Schroder report said. &quot;That was the first week-to-week seasonally-adjusted decline in a month.&quot;</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1562</p>
</text>
